{"id": "striviaqa0248", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Ming Dynasty ruled from the 14th to the 1 7th century. It was founded by Zhu Yuanzhang, who became Emperor Hongwu in 1368 after over throwing the Mongol-led Yuan Dynasty. During its time, the Ming saw major cultural, economic, and military achievements, like the construction of the Forbidden City and voyages led by Zheng He. The dynasty ended in 164 4 when the last emperor, Chongz heng, fled as Manchu forces took control, marking the beginning of the Qing Dynasty.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
